CASE = [
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> The motto of the Supreme Court, Yato Dharmastato Jayah, is taken from the Mahabharata. In 2023 the Sengol was placed in the new Parliament building. Ancient thinkers spoke of rajadharma, the duty of the king to protect the people. Today we say that government decides 'who governs' while governance is about 'how' governing is done. "
   "(i) From which epic is the motto of the Supreme Court taken? (ii) What does rajadharma mean? (iii) Which term focuses on 'who governs'? (iv) Why is governance considered wider than government?",
   "(i) The Mahabharata (1). (ii) The duty of the king to protect the people (1). (iii) Government (1). (iv) Governance includes decision-making, implementation and monitoring, and involves citizens, civil society, media and private bodies besides the government (2).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> A resident of a village uploads her certificates on DigiLocker. The panchayat buys equipment through GeM and a villager files a complaint on CPGRAMS and tracks its status. However, some families in the village cannot use these services because there is no reliable internet. "
   "(i) What is DigiLocker used for? (ii) Expand GeM. (iii) What is CPGRAMS used for? (iv) State one advantage and one limitation of e-governance shown here.",
   "(i) To store documents digitally (1). (ii) Government e-Marketplace (1). (iii) Redressal of grievances (complaints) (1). (iv) Advantage: services become faster and more transparent (1); limitation: lack of internet or digital skills excludes some people (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
 Q("<b>Case study.</b> The National Education Policy 2020 was prepared under the chairmanship of Dr K. Kasturirangan. Khelo Bharat Niti 2025 coordinates sports policy across the Union, states, districts and blocks, with Model Sports Districts created at the district level. A district office runs a scheme for meals but no one tracks its results. "
   "(i) Who chaired the committee that prepared NEP 2020? (ii) At which level is a Model Sports District created? (iii) What does a scheme provide, compared with a policy? (iv) Which step of the policy cycle is missing in the district, and why is it needed?",
   "(i) Dr K. Kasturirangan (1). (ii) District level (1). (iii) A scheme gives concrete benefits, while a policy only sets the direction (1). (iv) Monitoring and evaluation (1); it tracks progress, ensures accountability and gives feedback for improving the scheme (1).", "1+1+1+2"),
]

